This riso animation is a playful yet poignant reimagining of the Wicked Witch of the West as she transforms into Glinda. It examines the fluidity of identity and seeks to challenge the rigid archetypes often imposed on older women in storytelling. By juxtaposing the fluorescent risograph colors, the work explores how society frequently confines female figures to polarized roles\'97sinister sorceress or benevolent beauty\'97unveiling the complexity beneath these oversimplified caricatures.\
